guide forever/horde/30-40/02-stranglethorn-vale
title Stranglethorn Vale
faction Horde
levels 32-38
zone Stranglethorn Vale
next forever/horde/30-40/03-arathi-highlands

# Consensus route (Horde Tauren export), visit 24 (Stranglethorn Vale
# 32.9-37.4), plus the export's earlier Stranglethorn stop (visit 17,
# level 30.4), shared by every Horde start. Era + known Forever quests only.
# The October refresh's export (visit 22, 32.9-37.4) has the same quests,
# with the 30.4 stop already folded in; no Forever-only quest is picked
# here. (Forever above 30 cannot be checked in game until launch on 4
# November: this guide follows the data, not play.)
#
# Flow: the Undercity (where the previous guide ends) -> zeppelin to Grom'gol
# (flight path, bind) -> Nesingwary's camp -> young tigers and panthers ->
# Nesingwary -> tigers, panthers, raptors and the Bloodscalp trolls ->
# Nesingwary (Panther Mastery, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn) -> elder
# tigers and Lashtail raptors -> Grom'gol -> Nesingwary and Sin'Dall -> the
# Bloodscalp village -> hearth to Grom'gol -> the road south to Booty Bay
# (flight path) -> fly to Grom'gol -> the river, the basilisks and the
# Bloodscalp village -> Grom'gol -> fly to Booty Bay -> fly to Grom'gol ->
# Lashtail raptors -> Mosh'Ogg, Shadowmaw and the Snapjaw river -> Grom'gol
# -> the Vile Reef -> the Bloodscalp ruins -> Grom'gol -> pages from the
# trolls -> Shadowmaw panthers -> Nesingwary -> hearth to
# Grom'gol -> Jungle Stalkers on the coast -> Grom'gol -> Mistvale gorillas
# -> Booty Bay (Hostile Takeover, bind) -> fly to Grom'gol -> the Venture
# Co. camp -> hearth to Booty Bay.
#
# Optional extras:
# - Crystal in the Mountains (635) starts from the Pendant of Myzrael, a
#   0.01-0.08% drop from the trolls; take it only if one drops (it ends in
#   Arathi).
# - The Green Hills of Stranglethorn (338-342): its pages drop at about 1%
#   each from the vale's trolls (or buy them); the export counts the hunt
#   for them. The chapters are accepted at Nesingwary's camp and turned in
#   later in this guide if you have them.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Welcome to the Jungle (583), Tiger Mastery (185) and Panther Mastery
#   (190) come from the old export's first Stranglethorn stop at 30.4,
#   merged here, as the refreshed export now does: the same camp, without
#   the zeppelin round trip from Orgrimmar. The Booty Bay flight path from
#   that stop is taken on the first Booty Bay visit.
# - One Grom'gol bind for most of the visit: the export's Booty Bay binds
#   are each replaced before use. The second hearth is replaced by the short
#   ride from the Bloodscalp village to Grom'gol.
# - Some Assembly Required (577): accepted and its skins gathered early, but
#   handed in on the Booty Bay stop later in this guide instead of an extra
#   Grom'gol-Booty Bay round trip.
# - The Vile Reef is done first, on the way north to the Bloodscalp ruins.
# - The export rebinds between Grom'gol and Booty Bay three times in its
#   last hour; only the Booty Bay bind that is used (hearth back for Hostile
#   Takeover) is kept.
# - Hostile Takeover's crystals are gathered right after turning in the
#   gorilla sinew at Grom'gol, on the ride north, instead of in a separate
#   trip.
# - The export takes the Hammerfall flight path and bind at the end of this
#   visit; they are at the start of forever/horde/30-40/03-arathi-highlands,
#   where you are actually in Hammerfall.
# - Panther Mastery (192) and The Green Hills of Stranglethorn (338-342) are
#   taken when the panthers of 191 are handed in, not on a ride from Grom'gol
#   up to Nesingwary's camp and back down to the Shadowmaw Panthers by
#   Grom'gol: the panthers are still hunted at the same point of the route.
#
# Class quests: Shamans make one hop to Kalimdor from Grom'gol once they are
# bound there: the zeppelin to Orgrimmar, a flight to Ratchet (the Shard of
# Water to Islen Waterseer, Call of Water 96: your Water Totem) and the
# hearth back. The quest started in forever/horde/30-40/01-desolace. The
# Warlock Felhunter's Damaged Chest stop (1803) moved with the rest of the
# chain to forever/class/warlock/felhunter-horde.
#
# Class training: Shamans train in Orgrimmar on their hop (about 33);
# otherwise none in Stranglethorn: the guide stays between Grom'gol and
# Booty Bay. You train next at about 37.5 at the start of the next guide, on
# the way through the Undercity (Hunters and Shamans in Orgrimmar, Druids in
# Thunder Bluff), and again in Orgrimmar at about 39.
#
# Carried on: Trollbane (638) for Arathi.
#
# Not taken: Marg Speaks (1261): Marg's note is offered only after The Troll
# Witchdoctor (1240), which is now turned in at Grom'gol in forever/horde/40-
# 50/01-stranglethorn-vale, after the Dustwallow stay.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Grom'gol

step Zeppelin to Grom'gol
  zone Tirisfal Glades
  tip Leave the Undercity by the lift and walk up through the ruins to the zeppelin towers; the Grom'gol zeppelin is the one on the south-west tower.
  goto 61.8,59.2 "Zeppelin towers"

step Grom'gol Base Camp
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip The zeppelin lands at the tower on the west side of the camp.
  getfp "Grom'gol" npc 1387           -- Thysta
  sethome "Grom'gol Base Camp" npc 5814 -- Innkeeper Thulbek
  accept 581                          -- Nimboya

step Orgrimmar
  only Shaman
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Take the Orgrimmar zeppelin from the tower on the west side of Grom'gol and train in the city before you fly on.
  train class

step Islen Waterseer
  only Shaman
  zone The Barrens
  tip Take the Orgrimmar zeppelin from the tower on the west side of Grom'gol and fly to Ratchet. Islen Waterseer camps on the coast a short ride south of it.
  fly "Ratchet"
  turnin 96                           -- Islen Waterseer: Healing Stream Totem and your Water Totem

step Back to Grom'gol
  only Shaman
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  hearth "Grom'gol Base Camp"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Nesingwary's camp

step Nesingwary's camp
  tip Follow the road north out of Grom'gol; Nesingwary's hunting camp sits on the hill north-east of the river. From here on, keep every page of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn you loot: Barnil asks for them later.
  accept 583                          -- Barnil Stonepot
  turnin 583                          -- Hemet Nesingwary
  turnin 5762
  turnin 5763
  accept 194
  accept 185                          -- Ajeck Rouack
  accept 190                          -- Sir S. J. Erlgadin

step Young tigers and panthers
  tip Young Stranglethorn Tigers prowl west of the camp, Young Panthers south and east of it.
  kill 681 quest 185
  kill 683 quest 190

step Nesingwary's camp
  turnin 185                          -- Ajeck Rouack
  accept 186
  turnin 190                          -- Sir S. J. Erlgadin
  accept 191

step Tigers and panthers
  tip Stranglethorn Tigers and Panthers (32-33) roam the hills east of the camp, along the lake shore.
  kill 682 quest 186
  kill 736 quest 191

step Raptors and the Bloodscalp trolls
  tip Head west past the camp. Stranglethorn Raptors (33-34) hunt the clearings, and the Bloodscalp trolls hold the ruins on the coast: every Bloodscalp can drop a tusk. A Pendant of Myzrael is a very rare drop from them: if one drops, read it.
  kill 685 quest 194
  collect 3901 quest 581
  collect 4614 x1 optional
  accept 635 optional

step Nesingwary's camp
  turnin 186                          -- Ajeck Rouack
  accept 187
  turnin 191                          -- Sir S. J. Erlgadin
  accept 192                          -- The Shadowmaw Panthers come much later, by Grom'gol
  accept 338 optional                 -- Barnil Stonepot
  accept 339 optional
  accept 340 optional
  accept 341 optional
  accept 342 optional
  turnin 194                          -- Hemet Nesingwary
  accept 195

step Elder tigers and Lashtail raptors
  tip The Elder Stranglethorn Tigers (34-35) roam the hills south-west of the camp; the Lashtail Raptors (35-36) hunt further south, towards Grom'gol.
  kill 1085 quest 187
  kill 686 quest 195

step Grom'gol
  tip Follow the road south to Grom'gol.
  turnin 581                          -- Nimboya
  accept 582

step Nesingwary's camp
  tip Back north to the camp.
  turnin 195                          -- Hemet Nesingwary
  turnin 187                          -- Ajeck Rouack
  accept 188

step Sin'Dall
  tip Sin'Dall, a level 37 tiger, prowls the hilltop south-west of the camp.
  collect 3879 quest 188 @31.8,16.4

step Nesingwary's camp
  turnin 188                          -- Ajeck Rouack

step Bloodscalp headhunters
  tip The Bloodscalp Headhunters (36-37) in the village on the coast carry the shrunken heads.
  collect 1532 quest 582

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Booty Bay

step Hearth to Grom'gol
  hearth "Grom'gol Base Camp"
  turnin 582                          -- Nimboya

step Booty Bay
  tip Follow the road south to Booty Bay at the southern tip of the vale and enter through the tunnel in the cliffs. Stay on the road: the jungle beside it is well above your level. Gringer, the Horde flight master, waits on the upper deck.
  getfp "Booty Bay" npc 2858          -- Gringer
  accept 189                          -- Kebok
  accept 201                          -- Krazek
  accept 605                          -- Crank Fizzlebub
  accept 575                          -- Drizzlik
  vendor nearest

step Fly to Grom'gol
  fly "Grom'gol"                      -- Gringer

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The north again

step The camp by the river
  tip Krazek's missing hunters' camp is Nesingwary's: walk among its tents and the investigation completes. River Crocolisks lie along the river below the camp.
  complete 201
  collect 4053 quest 575

step Basilisks and the Bloodscalp village
  tip West past the camp, Crystal Spine Basilisks (34-35) sit on the rocks; every Bloodscalp in the village beyond can drop an ear.
  collect 3918 quest 605
  collect 1519 quest 189

step Fly to Booty Bay
  tip Ride south down the coast to Grom'gol and fly to Booty Bay.
  fly "Booty Bay"                     -- Thysta
  turnin 575                          -- Drizzlik
  accept 577
  turnin 605                          -- Crank Fizzlebub
  turnin 201                          -- Krazek
  turnin 189                          -- Kebok

step Fly to Grom'gol
  fly "Grom'gol"                      -- Gringer
  accept 568                          -- Commander Aggro'gosh
  accept 570                          -- Far Seer Mok'thardin
  accept 638                          -- Nimboya: for Arathi, later on the route
  accept 596                          -- Kin'weelay
  accept 629

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Raptors, Mosh'Ogg, Shadowmaw

step Lashtail raptors
  tip The Lashtail Raptors (35-36) hunt the jungle just north-east of Grom'gol.
  kill 686 quest 568

step Commander Aggro'gosh
  turnin 568
  accept 569

step Mosh'Ogg camp
  tip The Mosh'Ogg ogres camp in the hills just east of Grom'gol. Kill one Brute and one Witch Doctor (36-37); pull them one at a time.
  kill 1142 quest 569.1
  kill 1144 quest 569.2

step Shadowmaw jungle and the Snapjaw river
  tip East of the ogres, Shadowmaw Panthers (37-38) stalk unseen until they strike; the Stranglethorn Tigresses roam the same ground and now and then drop a pristine fang. Snapjaw Crocolisks line the river just west of the jungle; keep their skins for Drizzlik.
  collect 3838 quest 570.1
  collect 3839 quest 570.2
  collect 4104 quest 577 @39.9,28.4

step Grom'gol
  tip Back to Grom'gol.
  turnin 569                          -- Commander Aggro'gosh
  turnin 570                          -- Far Seer Mok'thardin
  vendor nearest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Vile Reef and the Bloodscalp ruins

step The Vile Reef
  tip North-west of Grom'gol the Vile Reef lies under the water off the coast. The Tablet Shard rests on the sea floor by the sunken ruins; watch your breath and the murlocs.
  collect 4094 quest 629 @24.8,22.9

step Bloodscalp ruins
  tip The Bloodscalp trolls hold the ruins up the coast north of the reef and the village beyond; every one can drop a Bloody Bone Necklace. Keep looting pages of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn.
  collect 3915 quest 596

step Grom'gol
  tip Ride back south to Grom'gol.
  turnin 596                          -- Kin'weelay
  turnin 629

step Green Hills pages
  tip Pages of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn drop at about 1% each from the Bloodscalp and Skullsplitter trolls; keep every page you loot and look on the auction house for the rest. Barnil takes the chapters later in this guide.
  collect 2725 quest 339.1 optional
  collect 2728 quest 339.2 optional
  collect 2730 quest 339.3 optional
  collect 2732 quest 339.4 optional
  collect 2734 quest 340.1 optional
  collect 2735 quest 340.2 optional
  collect 2738 quest 340.3 optional
  collect 2740 quest 340.4 optional
  collect 2742 quest 341.1 optional
  collect 2744 quest 341.2 optional
  collect 2745 quest 341.3 optional
  collect 2748 quest 341.4 optional
  collect 2749 quest 342.1 optional
  collect 2750 quest 342.2 optional
  collect 2751 quest 342.3 optional

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Panther Mastery

step Shadowmaw panthers
  tip The Shadowmaw Panthers (37-38) stalk the jungle east of the Mosh'Ogg hills and north-east towards the lake; they strike from stealth. Loot every Green Hills page you find on the way.
  kill 684 quest 192

step Green Hills pages
  tip Pages of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn drop at about 1% each from the Bloodscalp and Skullsplitter trolls; take what drops and check the Auction House for the rest.
  collect 2725 quest 339.1 optional
  collect 2728 quest 339.2 optional
  collect 2730 quest 339.3 optional
  collect 2732 quest 339.4 optional
  collect 2734 quest 340.1 optional
  collect 2735 quest 340.2 optional
  collect 2738 quest 340.3 optional
  collect 2740 quest 340.4 optional
  collect 2742 quest 341.1 optional
  collect 2744 quest 341.2 optional
  collect 2745 quest 341.3 optional
  collect 2748 quest 341.4 optional
  collect 2749 quest 342.1 optional
  collect 2750 quest 342.2 optional
  collect 2751 quest 342.3 optional

step Nesingwary's camp
  turnin 192                          -- Sir S. J. Erlgadin
  turnin 339 optional                 -- Barnil Stonepot
  turnin 340 optional
  turnin 341 optional
  turnin 342 optional
  turnin 338 optional

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- South: stalkers, gorillas

step Hearth to Grom'gol
  hearth "Grom'gol Base Camp"
  accept 572                          -- Far Seer Mok'thardin

step Jungle Stalkers
  tip The Jungle Stalkers (40-41) hunt the coast south of Grom'gol. They are well above you: pull one at a time and rest between fights.
  collect 3863 quest 572

step Far Seer Mok'thardin
  turnin 572
  accept 571

step Mistvale gorillas
  tip Take the road south towards Booty Bay. The Elder Mistvale Gorillas (40-41) live in Mistvale Valley, east of the road; about one in twenty carries an aged sinew.
  collect 3862 quest 571

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Booty Bay and the Venture Co.

step Booty Bay
  tip Follow the road on south into Booty Bay.
  sethome "Booty Bay"
  accept 213                          -- Kebok
  vendor nearest
  turnin 577                          -- Drizzlik: the Snapjaw skins gathered earlier

step Fly to Grom'gol
  fly "Grom'gol"
  turnin 571                          -- Far Seer Mok'thardin

step Venture Co. camp
  tip Ride north past Nesingwary's camp to the lake. The Venture Co. Geologists (34-36) work the camps along its western shore; they carry the Tumbled Crystals.
  collect 4106 quest 213

step Hearth to Booty Bay
  hearth "Booty Bay"
  turnin 213                          -- Kebok
  note The next guide flies you north to Tarren Mill and into the Arathi Highlands.
